        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: سارق",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سارق — sāriq — \"a robber\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ركض السارق بين السيارات. rakaḍa as-sāriq bayna as-sayyārāt. The robber ran between the cars."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural سارقون. لص is the everyday word; سارق (sāriq) is the one who stole."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سارق (sāriq) is built on the native Arabic root s-r-q (Lane), \"to take a thing secretly\". Sāriq is its active participle, \"one who steals\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
